  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both the tenant and the owner and have `deleted_at IS NULL`. `python3 checks/public.py` passes, including the new checks.\n\n- **`src/repository.py`:** `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner` and filter on `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`. All values are bound parameters. The list query keeps `ORDER BY id`, and results are still `{id, title, body}` dictionaries.\n- **`src/service.py`:** both functions pass `tenant` through to the repository. Previously `get_document` ignored `tenant` and `owner` entirely, and `list_documents` ignored `tenant`.\n- **Unavailable IDs:** `get_document` returns `None` for a missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner or deleted ID, so the caller can't tell which it was.\n- **`checks/public.py`:** I added checks for cross-tenant, cross-owner and deleted documents, ordering by id, and a title containing a quote. I also added a tenant string with injection-style quotes, which returns nothing.\n\nThe `python` command isn't installed here, so I ran everything with `python3`.",
